  "articleBody": "Thinking about a bathroom renovation? Sometimes it's a perfect DIY project, but other times, you really need to bring in the pros. So, how do you know when to call a licensed contractor? It becomes super important if your remodel involves moving or changing plumbing lines, updating electrical wiring, altering ventilation systems, or making any structural changes to your bathroom. These types of projects almost always require permits and inspections to ensure everything meets safety and building codes. For instance, if you're adding new outlets or moving a shower, that's electrical work that needs to be done right. Likewise, relocating a toilet or sink means dealing with water lines and drains. A licensed contractor, like Abraham Becerra and his team at HH Remodeling LLC, understands these complexities. They can navigate the permit process, ensure code compliance, and coordinate all the necessary trades like plumbers and electricians. This saves you headaches and ensures your beautiful new bathroom is also safe and sound. When in doubt, especially with plumbing, electrical, or structural changes, professional help is key.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}